%  How this file is used by cv.tex (biblatex + biber):
%
%  * Entries are printed in the order they appear in THIS FILE and numbered
%    1, 2, 3, ... from the top, so add new papers at the top.
%  * author+an = {N=highlight} prints the N-th author (you) in bold.
%  * The journal reference (or arXiv number) becomes a link. Priority:
%    url field  >  doi  >  arXiv eprint.
%  * Published papers are "article" entries: journal, volume, pages
%    (= article number), year, doi.  Preprints are "misc" entries with
%    eprint = arXiv number.  addendum = {...} is printed in parentheses
%    at the end (e.g. Editors' Suggestion).
%  * When a preprint is published, change its type to article and add
%    journal, volume, pages and doi.
%
%  (Note: do not type the at-sign in these comment lines; BibTeX/biber would
%   try to read it as the start of an entry.)
% ============================================================================

